cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this formalization, please cite the software and record the full
  commit SHA used. For the mathematical results, also cite the paper listed
  under references. BibTeX entries are available in CITATION.bib.
type: software
title: >-
  LeanTransferDiscreteCarleman: A Lean 4 Formalization of
  Continuous-to-Fully-Discrete Carleman Estimates
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Yu
date-released: "2026-10-20"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MrGodfrey/LeanTransferDiscreteCarleman"
url: "https://github.com/MrGodfrey/LeanTransferDiscreteCarleman"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 and mathlib formalization of a transfer principle from continuous
  to fully discrete parabolic Carleman estimates, its P1 finite element and
  Cartesian finite difference realizations, and observability, control, and
  continuous null-control limits. The exact manuscript snapshot and proof
  coverage are documented in the repository. The bundled manuscript is
  excluded from the software license.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Carleman estimates
  - parabolic equations
  - finite elements
  - finite differences
  - observability
  - controllability
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: >-
      From Continuous to Fully Discrete Carleman Estimates:
      A Transfer Principle for Parabolic Schemes
    authors:
      - family-names: Lü
        given-names: Qi
      - family-names: Wang
        given-names: Yu
    year: 2026
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.02983"
    notes: >-
      arXiv:2610.02983 [math.NA]. The formalization follows the manuscript
      snapshot bundled in paper/; see paper/SOURCE_MANIFEST.md.
